From: Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: stream: Don't wait for the RX ring to empty on
 close

tbstream_dev_stop() flushes the RX ring with a 500 ms timeout before
stopping it. tb_ring_flush() waits for the ring's in-flight list to
empty, but an RX ring keeps its buffers posted to the controller (they
are posted again as soon as they are read), so the wait always runs into
the timeout. Every close of a stream device therefore takes at least
half a second, and an open of the same device, which takes sdev->lock,
waits for it: a program that closes its stream and opens it again, or a
new program that takes over the device, starts half a second late.

Stop the RX ring right away, as the busy-polling path already does.
Frames that arrive in the meantime are freed with the ring, as they are
after the timeout now: nothing reads them once the device is closed.

Fixes: 6db21d817b43 ("thunderbolt: Add support for USB4STREAM")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
@@ -677,7 +677,11 @@ static void tbstream_dev_stop(struct tbstream_dev *sde
 	} else {
 		tb_ring_flush(sdev->tx_ring.ring, 500);
 		tb_ring_stop(sdev->tx_ring.ring);
-		tb_ring_flush(sdev->rx_ring.ring, 500);
+		/*
+		 * The RX ring keeps its buffers posted to the controller,
+		 * so waiting for it to empty would only run into the
+		 * timeout.
+		 */
 		tb_ring_stop(sdev->rx_ring.ring);
 	}
 
